# Secrets. Two deploy keys already sit untracked in the repo root; without this rule a
# single `git add -A` publishes a private key to the remote, which is unrecoverable —
# rotating the key is the only real remedy once it has been pushed.
*.pem
*.key
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example

# Private KYC uploads (gov ID scans, selfies, video testimony) written by the local-disk
# StorageProvider adapter. These are the most sensitive bytes the app touches.
private-uploads/
